                <pb facs="0884" n="874" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg874"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/11–948: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Callanan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-11-09T17:00:00+08:00">November 9, 1948—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 9—5:41 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>133. Warning similar to Consulate General Shanghai sent to Americans today—this
                    district north of and bordering on Yangtze.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Callanan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
